    {
      "title": "Spain frees wealthy US-sought activist on bail as Irish police raid Dublin home",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/20/james-fergie-chambers-bail-spain",
      "description": "<p>Pro-Palestinian donor James ‘Fergie’ Chambers released as court considers extradition request</p><p>In a blur of events surrounding the Trump administration’s effort to extradite James “Fergie” Chambers, Spain released the wealthy US activist and donor on bail even as Irish police raided a Dublin house owned by Chambers and his partner, Stella Schnabel, acting on a request from US authorities.</p><p>Chambers’s case is the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jul/18/fergie-chambers-stella-schnabel-spain-extradition\">first known instance</a> of the US seeking to extradite a citizen over alleged support for Hamas, an accusation apparently tied to an international money-laundering charge in the criminal complaint underpinning the extradition request and donations to organizations helping Palestinians in Gaza.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/20/james-fergie-chambers-bail-spain\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-20T18:34:13"
    },
    {
      "title": "Spain court grants bail to pro-Palestinian activist James ‘Fergie’ Chambers",
      "link": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/20/spain-court-grants-bail-to-pro-palestinian-activist-james-fergie-chambers?traffic_source=rss",
      "description": "Chambers left Aranjuez prison near Madrid on Friday afternoon, shortly after Spain&#039;s High Court ordered him released.",
